        "ggPTQ4b2Oyp_text": "<strong>The Biggest Mistake Dog Owners&nbsp;</strong><br><span style=\"color:#DD1818;\"><strong>Make With Crusty Eyes</strong></span>",
        "ggUD4YdXUjF_text": "<p>Those brown tear stains you see every morning? Most owners think they're just cosmetic.&nbsp;<strong>They're not.</strong></p><p>That crusty buildup is bacteria, debris, and allergens accumulating in the warm, moist area around your dog's eyes. And when it sits there day after day, here's what happens:</p><p><strong>Days 1–7:</strong>&nbsp;Bacteria multiplies. Stains darken and become harder to remove.</p><p><strong>Weeks 2–3:</strong>&nbsp;Irritation and redness appear. Your dog starts rubbing their face — introducing more bacteria.</p><p><strong>Week 4+:</strong>&nbsp;What started as cosmetic turns into inflammation. Left untreated, this leads to infections requiring expensive vet visits.</p><p>The problem isn't that you're ignoring it.&nbsp;<strong>Most cleaning methods actually make it worse.</strong></p>",
        "gg7zWXq-7qs_text": "<p><i><strong>Most dog owners try 3-5 different products before finding one that actually works</strong></i></p>"
      }
